# Code standard

How a file is written once `standard-module` has said where it goes. Prettier and ESLint run on every edit (sensor), so this file has no formatting rules: only what a tool cannot catch.

## Language

- English for identifiers, comments, commit messages, Swagger text, log lines and exception messages.
- Legacy Portuguese text is translated when the line is touched, including exception messages. Clients branch on `code`, never on the message text. While decision D6 in `app/docs/decisions.md` (production usage map) is open, a translated message on a `/public/*` route is listed in the PR as a behavioral change.

## Types

- `strictNullChecks` and `noImplicitAny` are on. `any` is forbidden: use `unknown` and narrow, or type the boundary (Prisma `Json`, external payloads) with a parser.
- `as unknown as` only inside a mapper, on a Prisma `Json` column. `as` elsewhere means the type is wrong upstream.
- The non-null `!` appears only in DTO declarations (`public cpf!: string`). Never on an expression.
- Enums are string enums with PascalCase members and the persisted value as the value, as in `CredentialStatus.Active = "ACTIVE"`. Unions of literals are for values that are never persisted.
- Ids are the `Id` value object from `@src/shared/value-objects`, never a bare string, from the command inward. The controller receives the string and the command carries it as is; the handler wraps it.

## Nullability

- Absence that is legitimate in the domain is `T | null`, and the code branches on it explicitly. `undefined` and `?` exist only on input DTOs and params.
- Never manufacture a default to silence the type (`?? ""`, `?? 0`, `?? new Date(0)`). If a value is required, throw; if it is optional, carry the `null`.
- Entity props are complete: every field is set in the constructor from `create` or `restore`, none is assigned later from outside.

## Imports

- Absolute only: `@src/...` in `src`, `@test/...` in tests. ESLint blocks relative paths.
- `import type` for anything used only as a type.
- Order: Node built-ins, packages, `@src`, `@test`. One blank line between groups.
- Nothing from `@src/infra/database/@prisma/generated` outside `infra/` folders and DAOs.

## Classes

- Every member has an explicit access modifier, including constructors and `readonly` fields.
- Entity body order: private fields, private constructor, getters, static `create` (or the domain verb: `issue`), static `restore`, transitions (`revoke`, `approve`), predicates (`isX`, `ensureX`), private helpers.
- Handlers, services and gateways expose one public method per responsibility; a class with more than one public method that does not share state is two classes.
- Static-only classes are formatters and mappers; everything else is an injectable.

## Errors

- The domain throws `DomainError` subclasses from `@src/shared/errors`: `NotFoundError`, `ConflictError`, `InvalidStateError`, `ForbiddenError`, `ValidationError`. Each takes a stable `code` (`CREDENTIAL_NOT_FOUND`), a message for developers and optional `details` that are logged and never returned. `DomainErrorFilter` in `src/infra/http` maps them to HTTP. Entities never import `@nestjs/common`.
- Legacy entities throw `BadRequestException` directly; when such a line is touched, replace it with the domain error.
- `HttpException` subclasses are for the `api/` layer only: auth failures, throttling, malformed requests the DTO could not express.
- Never expose stack, SQL, XDR or chain payloads in a response.
- `try/catch` only when the catch does something: maps an external error, adds context, or decides a fallback. A catch that only rethrows or only logs is removed.

## Async

- `return await` only inside `try/catch`. Elsewhere return the promise.
- No floating promises: every promise is awaited, returned or explicitly `void`ed with a reason in a comment.
- Independent I/O runs in `Promise.all`; dependent I/O runs in sequence. Never a loop with an `await` per row where a batch call exists.

## Logging

- `Logger` from `@nestjs/common` with the class name as context. `console.*` exists only in `main.ts` and `src/scripts/`.
- Never log a secret, a signed XDR, a private input, a full VC document, a CPF or an API key. Log ids, hashes and status.
- One log line per business fact at `log` level; `debug` for steps inside a fact; `warn` for a handled anomaly; `error` only with the error object attached.
- Request-level ingress and egress logging lives in `src/infra/logging/` and is not wired yet (TD-004). Do not hand-roll per-request logs in handlers or controllers to compensate; the fix is wiring the loggers.

## DTOs and outputs

- Inputs are classes in `api/{context}/inputs/` with `class-validator` and `@ApiProperty` on every field: `public x!: T` when required, `public x?: T` when optional. Validation lives here, never in the handler.
- `/public/*` handlers return an explicit output type declared next to the handler or in `{module}.output.ts`, never an entity or a Prisma row: the shape is a contract. Backoffice and admin query handlers may return the DAO row.
- Trim and normalize input once, at the DTO with a transformer, not in the handler.

## Comments

- No comment that narrates the code (`// increment counter`). A comment states a constraint, a non-obvious reason or an external quirk.
- JSDoc on public ports (`domain/*.gateway.ts`, `*.repository.ts`) and on wrappers of external libraries.
- No deferred-work comments (`TODO`, `FIXME`, `later`, `for now`). Work that is not done goes to `app/docs/tech-debt.md` or to a Track task, where it has an owner and a trigger. A comment in code has neither.
